        "authoredProperties": {
          "displayName": {
            "t": "string",
            "v": "Stele: The Physics of Sunlit Mist"
          },
          "stele.inscription": {
            "t": "string",
            "v": "SANCTUARY OF SUNLIT MIST\n--------------------------------------\nBefore you unfolds the living synthesis of Volumetric Light Beams shining through atmospheric mist:\n\n1. LIGHT: A warm celestial source (diffuse 3.8, intensity 3.0, gold tint [1.0, 0.88, 0.65]) positioned at the zenith.\n2. MEDIUM: Suspended participating mist governed by OntoMath fields:\n   - Extinction (sigma_t = 0.28): Gradual exponential attenuation along the view and light rays.\n   - Scattering (sigma_s = 0.25): High single-scattering albedo (~0.89) imparting radiant luminosity.\n   - Chroma (C_v = [0.95, 0.97, 1.0]): Pristine atmospheric particulate tone.\n3. SPACE & OCCLUSION: An authored SDF clerestory aperture wall (SDF CSG subtraction)\n   carves three high window openings, casting distinct volumetric shafts into the hall.\n4. SHADOW & PENUMBRA: Bounded sphere-tracing evaluates source visibility (V = 1 inside the beams,\n   V = 0 in deep colonnade shadow), with soft penumbra transitions at the beam boundaries.\n5. PHASE FUNCTION: Henyey-Greenstein forward-scattering (g ~ 0.55) intensifies radiance\n   when looking toward the sunlit aperture.\n\nAuthor: Zachary Zhang & Antigravity (First Mover)"
          }
        }
      }
